nd horizontal lines represent hazard ratios (change in risk with each addition of the rare allele) and their confidence intervals. Sizes of the squares reflect the minor allele frequencies. <italic>P</italic>=<italic>P</italic>-value for an association of each tagSNP with endometrial cancer survival. <italic>P</italic><sub>win</sub>=<italic>P</italic>-value from a model including a window of five tagSNPs (the <italic>P</italic>-value aligns with the middle tagSNP of each window) for an association with endometrial cancer survival.</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" mime-subtype="eps" xlink:href="6604984f2"/></fig><table-wrap id="tbl1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p content-type="table-title">Selected characteristics of the cases and controls participating in the present endometrial cancer study</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups" border="1" width="85%"><colgroup><col align="left"/><col align="center"/><col align="center"/><col align="center"/></colgroup><thead valign="bottom"><tr><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Entire study</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Cases/controls (<italic>n</italic>)</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Cases/controls (mean)</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold><italic>P</italic><sup>a</sup></bold></th></tr></thead><tbody valign="top"><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">Age (years)</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">713/1567</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">64.0/62.8</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x0003c;0.0001</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">Age at menopause (years)</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">624/1508</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">51.0/50.1</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x0003c;0.0001</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">Recent BMI (kg/m<sup>2</sup>)<sup>b</sup></td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">712/1550</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">27.4/25.5</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x0003c;0.0001</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">Age at last birth (years)</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">610/1408</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">29.4/30.4</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.0006</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">Parity</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">713/1567</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">1.9/2.1</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x0003c;0.0001</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Cases only</bold></td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold><italic>n</italic> (&#x00025;)</bold></td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Endometrial cancer deaths (<italic>n</italic>)<sup>c</sup></bold></td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Mortality rate<sup>d</sup></bold></td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">Total cases</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">713</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">41</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.0064</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><italic>Endometroid tumours</italic></td><td align="char" valign="top" char="(" charoff="50">661 (92.7)</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">30</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.0050</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x02003;Grade 1</td><td align="char" valign="top" char="(" charoff="50">256 (38.7)</td><td align="