/label><p>From the date of diagnosis until 31 December 2004 or until date of emigration, whichever came first. Calculated as endometrial cancer deaths per person-year of follow-up.</p></fn><fn id="t1-fn6"><label>e</label><p>No: No invasion or &#x0003c;50&#x00025; of the myometrum. Yes: Invasion through &#x02a7e;50&#x00025; of the myometrium or through the serosa.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="tbl2" position="float"><label>Table 2</label><caption><p content-type="table-title">Genotyping results and SNP coverage in <italic>ESR1</italic> and <italic>EGF</italic></p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups" border="1" width="85%"><colgroup><col align="left"/><col align="center"/><col align="center"/></colgroup><thead valign="bottom"><tr><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>ESR1</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>EGF</bold></th></tr></thead><tbody valign="top"><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">Successfully genotyped SNPs<sup>a</sup> (<italic>n</italic>)</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">228<sup>b</sup></td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">104<sup>c</sup></td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">Polymorphic SNPs (<italic>n</italic>)</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">184</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">66</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">Common SNPs<sup>d</sup> (<italic>n</italic>)</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">165</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">55</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">SNPs deviating from HWE<sup>e</sup> (<italic>n</italic>)</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">8</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">1</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">SNPs ultimately included in our study (<italic>n</italic>)</td><td align="center" valign="